# Lua Component Scripting

Components are Lua files returning a spec table. CodeExecutionSystem auto-loads them on startup.

## Component Template
```lua
return {
  name = "My Component",
  category = "Power",            -- Power, Data, Production, Movement, Structure
  description = "What it does",
  icon = "icon-name.png",        -- from game-icons.net, white, no background
  attributes = {
    my_attr = {
      title = "Display Name",
      description = "Tooltip",
      type = AttributeType.FLOAT, -- INT | FLOAT | STRING | BOOL
      value = 1.0,
      -- optional easing: { type = AttributeEasingType.SIN, range = 0.1, period = 1000.0 }
    },
  },
  state = ComponentState.DEACTIVATED,
  size = ComponentSize.S,         -- S | M | L
  require = {},                   -- must coexist with
  conflict = {},                  -- cannot coexist with
  api = {
    myMethod = function(self)
      return attr(self, "my_attr")
    end,
  },
}
```

## Attribute Access
Use the `attr` / `setAttr` helpers — they work on both `Component` and `Frame`:
```lua
attr(self, "key")          -- get final (eased) value; nil if attribute missing
setAttr(self, "key", v)    -- set base value
-- Direct access (advanced):
self.data.attributes["key"]:GetBaseValue()
```

## Component Locator
Use `locator(frame, selector)` / `locatorAll(frame, selector)` instead of the individual
`getComponentByType` / `getComponentByName` methods. Supported selector formats:
```lua
locator(frame, "type:Propulsion")   -- by type attribute
locator(frame, "name:Motor")        -- by component name
locator(frame, ".Propulsion")       -- CSS shorthand for type
locator(frame, "#42")               -- by component id
locator(frame, { type = "Sensor" }) -- table form
locatorAll(frame, ".Storage")       -- returns a list of all matches
```

## Available Globals
Always in scope: `frame` (owning Frame), `environment`, `frameWorld`, `nexus`, `oracle`.

Grid step constants:
```lua
subcellStep()   -- 25 px — smallest move unit
cellStep()      -- 75 px — one full grid cell
```

UI feedback (standalone helpers):
```lua
showToast(msg, type)                     -- type: "info" | "warning" | "error"
setMapMarker(x, y, label, color)
clearMapMarkers()
removeMapMarker(label)
setGlobalIndicator(key, label, value, color)
```

World actions are **not** global — access them through component APIs:
- `Propulsion.api.move(frame, dir)` wraps `frameWorld.moveFrame`
- `Lidar.api.scan(frame)` wraps `frameWorld.scanAdjacent`
- `NearFieldCommunicator.api.getConnectedFrames(frame)` wraps `frameWorld.nfcFrames`

When implementing a new component that needs world access, use dot notation with explicit self:
```lua
frameWorld.moveFrame(frameWorld, frame.data.id, "N", subcellStep(), 1.0, 25.0)
frameWorld.scanAdjacent(frameWorld, frame.data.id)
frameWorld.nfcFrames(frameWorld, frame.data.id, 5)
```

Full reference: `docs/lua-api.md`.

## Data Packets
```lua
self:send({ destination = frame_id, body = "payload", headers = {} })
local pkt = self:read()   -- nil if empty
```

